.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-05-14T17:59:14Z","updated_at":"2021-05-14T17:59:14Z","body":"steps are:\r\n\r\n1. add dbapi_connection and dialect to ExceptionContext.   \"engine\" and \"connection\" can now be None in some cases\r\n2. move handle_error to be part of DialectEvents.  nothing else needs to change here and existing code that links the event from an Engine will be the same.  Connection will still call upon the handler as always.\r\n3. move the production of the ExceptionContext and actually running the hook from engine/base into defaultdialect\r\n3. in DefaultDialect.do_ping(), catch exceptions and call the same hook we created in step 3, where it will call upon ExceptionContext without an Engine or Connection\r\n4. update docs to indicate Engine / Connection may be None for the do_ping handler, maybe others, look more to dbapi_connection and Dialect for forwards compat.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/841409237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gr